tats":{"hp":12000,"atk":300,"def":150,"res":50,"elementalRes":null,"elementalDamageRes":null,"attackInterval":5}},"decaying_collector_disciple":{"slug":"decaying_collector_disciple","name":"Decaying Collector Disciple","icon":"/enemies-icons/Decaying Collector Disciple.webp","rank":"Elite","race":"Drone","movement":"Flying","attackPosition":null,"damageType":["No Damage"],"flavourText":"An organic construct containing the Nachzehrer King's Originium Arts. It can extract all kinds of dead souls from the battlefield to create Seeds of Decay.","abilities":["Flying unit.","Periodically summons several <Seeds of Decay>"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.3,"stats":{"hp":35000,"atk":500,"def":300,"res":35,"elementalRes":null,"elementalDamageRes":null,"attackInterval":5}},"trilby_asher":{"slug":"trilby_asher","name":"'Trilby Asher'","icon":"/enemies-icons/'Trilby Asher'.webp","rank":"Elite","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"'Forever honor one's commitments,' the proud motto of House Caster. While the Duke's military and political might are more than enough to back their word, the 'Trilby Ashers' are the real reason why the Duke of Caster's words hold any weight.","abilities":["After several attacks, moves towards the next checkpoint for the next attack"],"levelCount":1,"level":0,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.7,"stats":{"hp":36000,"atk":2250,"def":500,"res":35,"elementalRes":null,"elementalDamageRes":null,"attackInterval":6}},"damazti_cluster_enemy_1542_wdslm":{"slug":"damazti_cluster_enemy_1542_wdslm","name":"'Damazti Cluster'","icon":"/enemies-icons/'Damazti Cluster'.webp","rank":"Boss","race":null,"movement":"Ground","attackPosition":"Melee","damageType":["Physical"],"flavourText":"A long-lived that has drifted away from the Sarkaz Royal Court. They have taken the rise and fall of the various races as a sort of life experience, but the Damazti Cluster has yet to find the answer to what 'living' means.","abilities":["Spy","Whenever a certain percentage of HP is lost, summons an Isomorphic Fragment on an Operator or on the field that shares HP with self;","Both the Damazti Cluster and Isomorphic Fragments take reduced Physical and Arts damage for every Isomorphic Fragment present on the field","Both the Damazti Cluster and Isomorphic Fragments are Invulnerable while their identities have yet to be revealed","Attacks inflict Corrosion","First Form","Periodically releases [Derivative Iteration]: both the Damazti Cluster and Isomorphic Fragments simultaneously deal Physical damage to a target","When defeated for the first time, deals continuous Arts damage to all units around Damazti Cluster or Isomorphic Fragments while regenerating itself","Second Form","Periodically releases [Lifeline Burst] which locks onto all allies on the field, and after a period of time deals Arts damage to the targets and any allies in the adjacent 4 tiles and summons a Deconstructed Distortion on the locked-on positions","When HP falls below a certain percentage during second form, summons an Isomorphic Fragment lurking amongst your operators, targeting an operator that will be forced off the battlefield after summoning is complete. Prioritizes units without allies in adjacent spaces"],"levelCount":2,"level":1,"levelAssumed":false,"statsOverridden":false,"moveSpeed":0.5,"stats":{"hp":150000,"atk":750,"def":900,"res":50,"elementalRes":null,"elementalDamageRes":null,"attackInterval":2.5}}},"dropIcons":{"4002":"/item-icons/originite_prime.png"},"previewFile":"h12-4.webp","emergency":null,"devices":[{"col":6,"description":"Recover 5 DP and raise 5 cost limit when defeated","hidden":false,"key":"trap_111_wdfarm","kind":"device","name":"Roadside Emergency Reserves","row":5},{"col":7,"description":"Recover 5 DP and raise 5 cost limit when defeated","hidden":false,"key":"trap_111_wdfarm","kind":"device","name":"Roadside Emerge